lly. Finally, I'd ask: if we ban boxing for its risks, should we also ban horseback riding (high risk of traumatic brain injury), rock climbing, or even contact sports like hockey? Most people would say no—because we value personal freedom and the good these activities bring. Boxing deserves the same respect. So I'm not confident that the benefits *always* outweigh the risks for every boxer. But I am confident that, when properly regulated and chosen voluntarily, boxing can be an ethical sport—one where the benefits of autonomy, discipline, and fulfillment justify the managed risk.
